		"origin": "guideline-authored",
		"purpose": "Canonical BENTO dashboard (R=md, dense). ONE canvas work Section holding: header row (h1 + description + primary actions, fill-left/hug-right) → inline critical alert → KPI grid (4 stat cards) → bento row A (66-33: region breakdown list-panel + compact chart-panel) → bento row B (50-50: incidents list-panel + activity list-panel). DENSITY/STYLE REFERENCE ONLY.",
		"designNotes": "A dashboard is a GRID of self-titled panels on ONE background, NOT a stack of full-width titled zebra sections. Every panel is an elevation-1 Card that owns its own h4 title; no per-panel h2 headers, no zebra. KPIs on top; heterogeneous panels side by side via column splits; charts compact in the narrow column; dense data as list panels; alerts inline under the header.",
		"spacingModel": "R = md. Grouped stacks = sm (R−1); tight inline pairs = xs (R−2); card padding / header→content = md; panels & rows = lg. Section spacing 'small', full width, single canvas.",
		"colorModel": "emphasis-100 for headings AND values; labels Small+Bold+muted; meta muted; delta/trend tinted via semantic; trend Icon fills color.icon (emphasis-70)."
	},
